{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Why\n\nA vocabulary migration that is not guarded regresses: the next author or generated prompt\nreintroduces the old heading and nothing notices. This story closes the epic by proving the\nlive vocabulary is gone and adding the check that keeps it gone — while ensuring the guard\ncannot fire on the frozen records and unrelated `O-RAN-SC` occurrences that must NEVER change.\n\n## What\n\nSweep for residual SC vocabulary and add a CI guard against reintroduction.\n\n## Scope\n\n- A guard script under `scripts/` (wired into the existing lint/CI gates) failing the build when\n  `Success Criteria` / `success criteria` / `success criterion` or a bare `SC` used as that\n  abbreviation appears in live source.\n- The residual in-scope site no other story owns: `src/rebar/llm/completion.py:288`, whose\n  docstring reads \"its success criteria are met across children\". That IS the criteria-heading\n  sense, so it must be renamed to \"acceptance criteria\". (ADDED during implementation: an\n  audit of `src/rebar/` for the epic's AC1 found this site assigned to NO child story — 35bc\n  covered detectors, 2aa6 the reviewer prompts, 93d0 the eval specs and 44c7 the guides/docs,\n  and none of them reaches `completion.py`. Without this the epic's AC1 cannot pass.)\n- Its allowlist, which must exempt:\n  - `tests/fixtures/jira/search.json` and `tests/fixtures/jira/comment_map.json` — recorded\n    Jira payloads/comment text (one contains \"parent SC\"); these are captured records and\n    editing them changes the thing under test.\n  - `docs/archive/`, `docs/experiments/` — historical material.\n  - Historical citations to a past ticket's numbered criterion:\n    `tests/scripts/reducer/test_reducer_reduce_all.py:120`,\n    `tests/interfaces/store/test_canonical_event_bytes.py:1`,\n    `tests/unit/test_code_review_artifact.py:414`.\n  - `O-RAN-SC` — the Linux Foundation telecom consortium — in `docs/adr/0021-replication-change-refs.md:13`,\n    `docs/adr/0022-g2p-in-container.md:13,21`, `docs/adr/0023-inbound-github-gerrit-ssh-vote.md:13`\n    and `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml:10`.\n  - `src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor_assets/dist/editor.js` — minified vendor bundle.\n  - The epic's four PERMANENT vocabulary carve-outs (see epic 1386 Scope, amended):\n    `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_T2.md` — \"a pilot with metrics, or stated success\n    criteria for a trial\", generic English about an EXPERIMENT succeeding, which story 2aa6's\n    AC6 REQUIRES to survive; and the `dod_uncertifiable` / \"definition-of-done\" wording in\n    `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_verifier.md`,\n    `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_verifier_agentic.md` and\n    `src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify_models.py` — a separate concept this epic defers.\n  - `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_criteria_heading_collapse.py` — the contract test added\n    by story 35bc. Every occurrence there is a NEGATIVE-CASE PROBE proving the heading is\n    inert (one asserts its ABSENCE from the code-review scope context), so it doubles as the\n    \"test that injects one\" AC1 requires.\n  - `docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md` — GENERATED from the criteria registry, so it echoes\n    T2's excluded prompt verbatim; the epic's amended AC5 pins it at exactly one match.\n\n## Approach\n\nBefore implementing the guard, run python -m rebar.llm.plan_review.registry regenerate-criteria-guide. This is expected to be a no-op on current main; it makes the generated guide dependency explicit and ensures the T2 prompt supplies the one allowed success-criteria match.\n\n\nThe guard matches the exact phrase case-insensitively, plus `\\bSCs?\\b` restricted to the paths\nwhere the abbreviation could plausibly mean Success Criteria (`src/rebar/llm/reviewers/`,\n`src/rebar/_guides/`, `criteria_routing.json`). Scoping the bare-token rule by PATH rather than\nby a global word-boundary match is what keeps `O-RAN-SC` out of it without a fragile negative\nlookahead.\n\nThe allowlist is a data file, not inline regex, so an exemption is reviewable as a diff.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Run python -m rebar.llm.plan_review.registry regenerate-criteria-guide, then confirm docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md contains the T2 section and exactly one allowed success-criteria match.\n\n- The guard fails on a deliberately reintroduced `## Success Criteria` in a live source file.\n- The guard PASSES on the current tree with the allowlist applied.\n- A test asserting the four `O-RAN-SC` sites and the two Jira fixtures do not trip it.\n- Verify the four `O-RAN-SC` occurrences are byte-identical to their pre-migration content.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `scripts/` carries a guard script wired into an existing CI gate; it exits non-zero on a\n      reintroduced `## Success Criteria` in live source (proven by a test that injects one).\n- [ ] The guard exits 0 on the migrated tree.\n- [ ] A test asserts the guard does NOT fire on the four `O-RAN-SC` sites, the two\n      `tests/fixtures/jira/` files, or the three historical-citation sites.\n- [ ] `git diff` against the pre-migration base shows the four `O-RAN-SC` occurrences and\n      `editor.js` unchanged.\n- [ ] A full-repo sweep confirms no live-source SC vocabulary remains outside the allowlist.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck` and the full pytest suite pass."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785269604800288001,"uuid":"5d8ce7dc-8fc0-4d2f-b12f-14ff0cf51861"}